1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:01,740
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:03,270
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:11,280
(Episode 38)

4
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:45,250
Ma'am.

5
00:00:47,090 --> 00:00:48,790
Am I a bit late?

6
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:51,320
No, I just got here myself.

7
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:00,060
Does it look weird?

8
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:03,440
I decided to splurge and bought it.

9
00:01:04,270 --> 00:01:05,900
Not at all, it looks great on you.

10
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:07,670
Shall we go?

11
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:09,340
Sure.

12
00:01:24,820 --> 00:01:28,990
Su Ah, it's pretty chilly today.
How about we skip the ice pop?

13
00:01:29,490 --> 00:01:31,430
No, I want an ice pop.

14
00:01:31,730 --> 00:01:33,900
Don't you ever want
something different, sweetie?

15
00:01:35,270 --> 00:01:38,070
It's Grandma.
Dad, look. It's Grandma.

16
00:01:41,870 --> 00:01:45,810
Hey, that is not your grandma.
Why would my mom ever wear...

17
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:47,350
I almost fell.

18
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:51,220
She is wearing that.

19
00:01:51,750 --> 00:01:54,320
- That really is my mom.
- Grandma looks so pretty.

20
00:01:54,690 --> 00:01:57,990
- That man with her looks cool too.
- Wait, what on earth is going on?

21
00:01:58,690 --> 00:01:59,960
Who is that guy with her?

22
00:02:00,990 --> 00:02:02,960
Where is she going
dressed like that?

23
00:02:03,030 --> 00:02:04,530
Who is that guy, anyway?

24
00:02:04,530 --> 00:02:06,230
- Mom. Hey, Mom.
- Daddy.

25
00:02:06,230 --> 00:02:08,000
What is it?

26
00:02:08,070 --> 00:02:09,630
I need to pee. Bathroom.

27
00:02:10,030 --> 00:02:11,640
Seriously? Right now?

28
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:16,540
- Can't you hold it for a bit?
- I really have to go.

29
00:02:23,110 --> 00:02:24,120
Oh, come on.

30
00:02:25,350 --> 00:02:27,490
I hear this show is
really popular right now.

31
00:02:27,650 --> 00:02:29,490
And as it turns out...

32
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:34,560
(Art Hall)

33
00:02:34,630 --> 00:02:36,360
Time just flew by during the show.

34
00:02:36,930 --> 00:02:38,200
I'm so glad we came.

35
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:42,600
A colleague told me
it's the hottest show right now.

36
00:02:42,830 --> 00:02:44,200
The house was completely packed
today too.

37
00:02:48,510 --> 00:02:49,910
(The House Beyond Waiting)

38
00:02:54,650 --> 00:02:55,650
Shall we?

39
00:02:56,410 --> 00:02:57,580
Sure.

40
00:03:11,430 --> 00:03:12,630
- Yes.
- Yes.

41
00:03:23,310 --> 00:03:24,940
When I was younger,
I could run around...

42
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:26,540
even in 7cm heels.

43
00:03:27,150 --> 00:03:28,810
Gosh, my heels.

44
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:35,850
Where did Dr. Ju go after telling me
to wait just a moment?

45
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:44,300
I'm back.

46
00:03:44,830 --> 00:03:46,230
Were you about to call me?

47
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:48,970
Yes, you were gone for so long.

48
00:03:50,070 --> 00:03:51,300
Where did you go?

49
00:03:54,470 --> 00:03:56,310
Did you go buy something?

50
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:59,710
Yes. Since we were out,

51
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:03,210
I remembered I needed to buy
a gift for a friend.

52
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:06,320
My friend has
rather particular taste,

53
00:04:07,450 --> 00:04:10,290
so finding the right gift
took a little longer than expected.

54
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:15,330
- I am sorry.
- So you went to pick out a gift.

55
00:04:15,930 --> 00:04:16,930
A friend?

56
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:19,100
Is it a girlfriend?

57
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,370
To leave someone waiting here
just to buy it...

58
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:26,740
Ma'am.

59
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:30,880
Yes, let us go.

60
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:32,510
Wait a moment.

61
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:34,710
Pardon?

62
00:04:36,650 --> 00:04:39,150
What are you doing?

63
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:49,060
Could you try these on for a moment?

64
00:04:49,460 --> 00:04:50,500
Me?

65
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:53,730
Why would I try on shoes
meant for someone else?

66
00:04:54,470 --> 00:04:56,330
The friend who will receive them...

67
00:04:56,970 --> 00:04:59,200
is very particular.

68
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:03,370
Please try them on first
to see if they look good.

69
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:07,450
We do not even know
if the size will fit...

70
00:05:08,150 --> 00:05:09,750
I think they will fit about right.

71
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:26,060
Why are you putting
my shoes in there?

72
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:28,800
Wouldn't it be uncomfortable
to carry them around?

73
00:05:32,140 --> 00:05:34,470
Please stand up
and walk around a bit.

74
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:39,610
You want me to walk around
in someone else's new shoes?

75
00:05:40,650 --> 00:05:42,610
You have to walk in them
to know if they are comfortable.

76
00:05:43,150 --> 00:05:45,120
And tell me how they feel.

77
00:05:59,330 --> 00:06:00,530
They are comfortable.

78
00:06:01,170 --> 00:06:02,170
And pretty.

79
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:03,600
What about your heels?

80
00:06:04,670 --> 00:06:05,740
They do not hurt.

81
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:08,210
Earlier, it chafed
with every step I took,

82
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:10,240
so honestly, less than five
minutes after leaving,

83
00:06:10,310 --> 00:06:11,610
I regretted wearing them.

84
00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:16,810
Why are you laughing?

85
00:06:17,950 --> 00:06:19,450
I guess you noticed.

86
00:06:20,250 --> 00:06:21,250
A little.

87
00:06:22,350 --> 00:06:25,660
Gosh, I broke a sweat trying
to pretend it did not hurt.

88
00:06:27,860 --> 00:06:29,190
Shall we go, then?

89
00:06:29,830 --> 00:06:30,830
Sure.

90
00:06:41,170 --> 00:06:42,740
I mean it.

91
00:06:43,140 --> 00:06:45,710
I went out of my way
to come see a play,

92
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:47,250
so why would I flatter you?

93
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:49,950
The acting was truly great today.

94
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:54,320
I clapped so hard toward the end
that my palms were stinging.

95
00:06:55,590 --> 00:06:57,560
If I had known
you would like it so much,

96
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:59,820
I should have brought you sooner.

97
00:07:00,690 --> 00:07:01,690
By the way...

98
00:07:01,760 --> 00:07:04,360
The actor who played
the grandfather earlier,

99
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:06,400
was he really your idol?

100
00:07:06,860 --> 00:07:07,970
I told you, he was.

101
00:07:08,730 --> 00:07:10,500
I have been a fan since I was young.

102
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:12,970
If I had not gotten married,

103
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:14,810
maybe I would be standing
on a stage like that...

104
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:16,610
with my idol today.

105
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:21,050
He was a judge
at a middle school drama festival,

106
00:07:21,410 --> 00:07:25,280
and he told me that I acted well
and should keep doing it.

107
00:07:26,450 --> 00:07:27,550
You do not believe me, do you?

108
00:07:27,950 --> 00:07:30,890
Not at all. Hearing you say it,

109
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,320
I can easily picture it.

110
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:37,090
In reality, well...

111
00:07:37,730 --> 00:07:39,330
I am just a middle-aged shopkeeper.

112
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:43,230
These days, senior models exist too.

113
00:07:43,470 --> 00:07:45,100
There is nothing stopping you,
even now.

114
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:46,440
What?

115
00:07:47,270 --> 00:07:50,710
That is easier said than done.
How could I act at my age?

116
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:53,910
Starting fresh
and taking on a challenge...

117
00:07:54,410 --> 00:07:56,080
I think that is the scariest part.

118
00:07:56,950 --> 00:07:58,480
No matter what it is.

119
00:08:01,950 --> 00:08:04,120
If I could really be born again,

120
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:06,590
in that life, I would definitely...

121
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:09,260
want to become an actress
on the stage.

122
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:15,000
Why wait until your next life
to chase your dream?

123
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:18,270
If you love it that much,

124
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:21,670
why not do it in this lifetime?

125
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,340
That is how I feel.

126
00:08:26,810 --> 00:08:30,150
You make everything sound
so easy, Dr. Ju.

127
00:08:30,150 --> 00:08:31,150
Well...

128
00:08:31,780 --> 00:08:32,850
Still, as for me,

129
00:08:34,290 --> 00:08:35,350
in this lifetime...

130
00:08:43,590 --> 00:08:45,130
Wait for me, ma'am.

131
00:08:46,430 --> 00:08:48,000
The person you have called...

132
00:08:49,330 --> 00:08:52,440
Why is she not answering?
How many times have I called now?

133
00:08:52,770 --> 00:08:54,040
Is it ringing?

134
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:57,440
Yes, I told you it is ringing.

135
00:08:58,440 --> 00:09:00,950
It is not turned off.
She is just not answering.

136
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:03,150
Can Mi Mi not hear it?

137
00:09:04,380 --> 00:09:05,380
Where on earth did she go,

138
00:09:05,450 --> 00:09:08,850
- and what is she doing?
- Exactly.

139
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:10,450
It is not like she is on a date...

140
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:13,060
- with some slick-looking guy.
- A guy?

141
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:14,530
Mi Mi has a man?

142
00:09:14,990 --> 00:09:16,030
A man?

143
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:17,930
What are you talking about?

144
00:09:18,830 --> 00:09:22,270
I was walking with Su Ah earlier,

145
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:24,770
and I saw Mom walking with some man.

146
00:09:25,570 --> 00:09:28,070
All dressed up in a style
she would never normally wear.

147
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:32,180
Do you not think Mom has been
acting really strange lately?

148
00:09:32,180 --> 00:09:35,110
So she really went out...

149
00:09:35,210 --> 00:09:36,250
wearing that outfit?

150
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,050
I thought she would return it.

151
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:44,720
Who on earth did she go out with?
Where did she go?

152
00:09:44,790 --> 00:09:47,530
I do not know, so I am calling her.

153
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:55,330
Mom, seriously, what is wrong?
Pick up the phone.

154
00:10:02,940 --> 00:10:04,040
(Kang Gang Nam, Eldest Son)

155
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:06,480
I might live like this now,

156
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:07,980
but back when I did
theater festivals,

157
00:10:08,050 --> 00:10:09,680
I really had that star quality.

158
00:10:11,350 --> 00:10:15,990
- Why the sudden look of doubt?
- Well, you are bragging so much.

159
00:10:17,490 --> 00:10:18,490
I am serious.

160
00:10:18,890 --> 00:10:21,860
When it came to dancing onstage,
I was phenomenal.

161
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:25,400
I completely blew the audience away.

162
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:30,200
Well, that works out perfectly.
Since you are wearing new shoes,

163
00:10:30,770 --> 00:10:32,600
why not show off those skills
from your prime?

164
00:10:33,870 --> 00:10:34,870
Right here?

165
00:10:37,210 --> 00:10:38,480
There is no audience anyway.

166
00:10:38,610 --> 00:10:41,810
- Are you nervous?
- There is nothing I cannot do.

167
00:10:42,550 --> 00:10:43,850
I have got new shoes on,

168
00:10:44,450 --> 00:10:46,180
so let me give it a little hop.

169
00:10:58,900 --> 00:10:59,930
I used to do things like this.

170
00:11:03,270 --> 00:11:05,270
One, two, one, two.

171
00:11:06,170 --> 00:11:07,170
Two...

172
00:11:07,670 --> 00:11:11,940
One, two, three.
Five, six. I can still do it!

173
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:14,350
I was really good at this.

174
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:21,990
Then I will put on
some music for you.

175
00:11:22,450 --> 00:11:24,690
You said those shoes
were comfortable,

176
00:11:25,390 --> 00:11:27,460
so give me a proper show.

177
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:30,030
Here comes the music.

178
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:08,400
Wait...

179
00:12:09,670 --> 00:12:10,870
Why are you stopping?

180
00:12:11,770 --> 00:12:12,970
Forget it.

181
00:12:13,470 --> 00:12:15,210
Someone might see us.

182
00:12:16,710 --> 00:12:20,640
Thanks to you, I feel like I watched
two plays today.

183
00:12:34,530 --> 00:12:36,860
(Jo Ri Ja)

184
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:49,340
Kang Da Mi, take this
to the sample room...

185
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:50,540
and ask them to make a pocket...

186
00:12:50,610 --> 00:12:53,280
that is 16cm wide and 18cm long.

187
00:12:53,780 --> 00:12:55,980
You mean 16 by 18?

188
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,280
Yes.

189
00:12:59,220 --> 00:13:02,250
Then by any chance,
are you taking my feedback?

190
00:13:07,630 --> 00:13:08,690
I mean...

191
00:13:08,890 --> 00:13:11,860
About how the pocket
was uncomfortable,

192
00:13:12,130 --> 00:13:13,730
did you take that into account?

193
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:20,100
Hurry along now.

194
00:13:21,270 --> 00:13:24,480
- Yes, do not worry, I will...
- Listen.

195
00:13:26,540 --> 00:13:29,510
I make the decisions,
and I'll take responsibility.

196
00:13:29,810 --> 00:13:32,150
So, Kang Da Mi,
just do as you are told.

197
00:13:33,820 --> 00:13:34,820
Yes, sir.

198
00:13:54,910 --> 00:13:59,080
What is his problem?
Would it kill him to say good job?

199
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:04,050
One minute he is nice,
and the next he turns so cold.

200
00:14:04,450 --> 00:14:05,780
He is so unpredictable.

201
00:14:10,590 --> 00:14:12,990
What? How is it this late already?

202
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:16,660
Can I even leave on time today
if the sample goes in now?

203
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:19,660
No, Kang Da Mi,

204
00:14:19,730 --> 00:14:21,300
should you really be worrying
about clocking out?

205
00:14:28,940 --> 00:14:30,470
I am back.

206
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,180
Well...

207
00:14:36,450 --> 00:14:37,510
Here, this...

208
00:14:38,250 --> 00:14:39,250
Yes. Go ahead and eat.

209
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:41,820
Pardon? Me?

210
00:14:41,990 --> 00:14:43,490
You need to eat to work, don't you?

211
00:14:44,460 --> 00:14:47,390
I am not an ox.
Why do you keep feeding me?

212
00:14:47,490 --> 00:14:48,990
Well, do not eat it
if you do not want to.

213
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:52,230
- I am not forcing you.
- It is not that I do not want it.

214
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:54,430
Thank you, I will enjoy it.

215
00:15:05,710 --> 00:15:09,180
Aren't you tired, sir?

216
00:15:10,180 --> 00:15:11,180
Not really.

217
00:15:12,450 --> 00:15:13,450
I see.

218
00:15:16,850 --> 00:15:18,660
You two have
very different personalities,

219
00:15:18,860 --> 00:15:20,760
but you are alike
when it comes to buying food.

220
00:15:22,590 --> 00:15:24,630
What? Who am I like?

221
00:15:25,730 --> 00:15:26,730
Team Leader Cha.

222
00:15:27,770 --> 00:15:28,770
Team Leader Cha?

223
00:15:29,970 --> 00:15:30,970
Do Yun?

224
00:15:35,210 --> 00:15:36,710
What does he buy you?

225
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:40,780
He buys me sushi and makes me tea.

226
00:15:41,410 --> 00:15:43,280
Your personalities are
completely different, though.

227
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:49,090
Team Leader Cha
gave me so much praise earlier.

228
00:15:49,090 --> 00:15:51,390
Give me a break. Praise for what?

229
00:15:51,790 --> 00:15:56,290
- For catching the pocket issue.
- He gets paid for doing nothing.

230
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:58,130
Going around
handing out compliments.

231
00:15:58,460 --> 00:16:01,230
Does he just have
too much time on his hands?

232
00:16:01,670 --> 00:16:03,970
Why do you always
have to say it like that?

233
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:08,910
Are both of you still working?

234
00:16:09,810 --> 00:16:11,040
Hey, do you even know what time...

235
00:16:11,140 --> 00:16:12,810
I mean, not you.

236
00:16:12,910 --> 00:16:14,610
Team Leader Cha,
what brings you here?

237
00:16:15,350 --> 00:16:18,180
Since our designer
decided to redo...

238
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:19,950
the product line for the first half
of next year,

239
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:22,690
our Product Planning team
is working overtime as well.

240
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:25,160
And?

241
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:27,560
Since things turned out this way,

242
00:16:27,830 --> 00:16:29,290
I thought we could share
a late-night snack.

243
00:16:31,130 --> 00:16:32,800
I will leave it here.
Eat before it gets cold.

244
00:16:33,630 --> 00:16:36,470
Looks delicious.
Thank you, Team Leader Cha.

245
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:39,670
Getting this kind of reception
for a box of pizza is not bad.

246
00:16:41,410 --> 00:16:42,470
Join us.

247
00:16:42,470 --> 00:16:45,040
- A whole pie is too much for us.
- Should I?

248
00:16:45,740 --> 00:16:47,280
May I, Head Designer?

249
00:16:53,780 --> 00:16:56,950
Just eat in moderation.
You cannot work if you are too full.

250
00:16:57,620 --> 00:17:00,060
I am not the type
to stuff myself foolishly.

251
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:03,430
Eat up.
You need energy to work late.

252
00:17:04,030 --> 00:17:06,260
Not too much, not too much.

253
00:17:07,330 --> 00:17:09,570
- No.
- Go ahead.

254
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:12,040
It is so good.

255
00:17:15,610 --> 00:17:16,610
Delicious, right?

256
00:17:18,210 --> 00:17:21,980
Who even eats pizza these days?
People eat sandwiches or something.

257
00:17:23,380 --> 00:17:24,980
You can have sandwiches and pizza.

258
00:17:29,990 --> 00:17:31,860
I was told to make her
quit on her own,

259
00:17:33,190 --> 00:17:34,630
but how do I get rid of her?

260
00:17:37,090 --> 00:17:38,300
Who are you getting rid of?

261
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:40,900
Pardon? Team Leader Cha.

262
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,730
You just said
you were getting rid of someone.

263
00:17:43,530 --> 00:17:45,440
Who is Assistant Manager Kang
getting rid of?

264
00:17:45,900 --> 00:17:47,000
Well...

265
00:17:48,010 --> 00:17:49,240
About the sneaker pop-up store.

266
00:17:50,110 --> 00:17:52,910
I was thinking about
how best to push out...

267
00:17:53,140 --> 00:17:54,650
the promotional press release.

268
00:17:55,450 --> 00:17:56,450
Is that so?

269
00:17:57,080 --> 00:17:58,250
Is there more to consider?

270
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:00,420
Did you not already compile
all the files...

271
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:01,690
and submit them
for approval earlier?

272
00:18:01,820 --> 00:18:03,650
I was wondering
if there was a better way.

273
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:06,760
I see. Let me know
once you have it figured out.

274
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,730
(Cha Do Yun, Team Leader)

275
00:18:30,210 --> 00:18:31,450
I am home.

276
00:18:32,620 --> 00:18:35,850
I had plans and went out,
so I am a bit late, Mother.

277
00:18:35,990 --> 00:18:37,690
I thought you would
come back tomorrow.

278
00:18:38,590 --> 00:18:39,890
Neglecting the restaurant,

279
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:41,790
where have you been
gallivanting around?

280
00:18:43,090 --> 00:18:44,700
Well, yes...

281
00:18:46,030 --> 00:18:47,260
Were there many customers?

282
00:18:48,570 --> 00:18:50,070
It was average.

283
00:18:50,830 --> 00:18:52,670
Still, you are the boss,

284
00:18:52,770 --> 00:18:54,470
so how could you be gone
for so long?

285
00:18:55,610 --> 00:18:58,940
Do you have any idea how hard it was
for Mrs. Choi and me?

286
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:00,880
You worked hard.

287
00:19:02,050 --> 00:19:03,610
Thank you for your
hard work, Mother.

288
00:19:04,380 --> 00:19:07,450
What are those shoes you brought in?

289
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:09,250
Did you buy shoes too?

290
00:19:10,090 --> 00:19:12,520
Have you decided to just
blow all your money now?

291
00:19:12,990 --> 00:19:15,230
You are making such a fuss
over just one outfit.

292
00:19:15,790 --> 00:19:17,730
No matter how busy you were
with your errands,

293
00:19:17,790 --> 00:19:19,060
you should have answered your phone.

294
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:21,600
We were waiting for you at home.

295
00:19:26,370 --> 00:19:27,910
I did not hear it ring, Mother.

296
00:19:28,370 --> 00:19:29,570
Ever since Kang Hak Sung's family...

297
00:19:30,810 --> 00:19:31,810
No,

298
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:34,610
ever since those people
came to our neighborhood,

299
00:19:34,610 --> 00:19:36,280
you have been acting so strange.

300
00:19:36,750 --> 00:19:37,750
Jo Ri Ja.

301
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:39,950
Is that not why you are doing this?

302
00:19:39,980 --> 00:19:42,190
Buying clothes and shoes
you never used to buy.

303
00:19:43,150 --> 00:19:44,420
Am I right?

304
00:19:47,490 --> 00:19:51,960
Well, good for you. You did well.
It is no way to live,

305
00:19:52,060 --> 00:19:53,600
wearing only work clothes
all the time.

306
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:57,730
Buy more clothes. Dress yourself up.
Should I buy you some?

307
00:19:57,940 --> 00:19:59,740
Shall we go to
the department store together?

308
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:03,370
Go and pick out
whatever you like, dear.

309
00:20:06,410 --> 00:20:08,610
You really do not have
to do that, Mother.

310
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:10,610
Since I bought this outfit,

311
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:11,920
I'll wear it
until it gets holes in it.

312
00:20:12,050 --> 00:20:13,380
Day in and day out.

313
00:20:14,890 --> 00:20:17,550
I am exhausted,
so I will go rest inside first.

314
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:21,460
Well, all right.

315
00:20:21,930 --> 00:20:24,760
I have no idea
what you were up to, though.

316
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:55,690
Dr. Ju, you should take
these shoes with you.

317
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,260
Why is that?

318
00:20:58,160 --> 00:20:59,530
I need to return them to you.

319
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:01,770
Thanks to you,
I got home comfortably.

320
00:21:02,130 --> 00:21:03,200
Please give me my shoes.

321
00:21:04,670 --> 00:21:08,770
You are great in every way, ma'am,
but you are completely oblivious.

322
00:21:09,370 --> 00:21:10,370
Pardon?

323
00:21:10,770 --> 00:21:12,910
Why do you think I bought flats?

324
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:15,710
You almost tripped when we met,
and you looked uncomfortable,

325
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:18,180
so I bought these shoes.

326
00:21:18,350 --> 00:21:19,550
As your physician,

327
00:21:19,550 --> 00:21:21,690
I just wanted you
to walk comfortably.

328
00:21:22,850 --> 00:21:24,960
You bought these for me?

329
00:21:26,990 --> 00:21:28,330
Still, I cannot just...

330
00:21:30,630 --> 00:21:31,730
No wonder.

331
00:21:32,300 --> 00:21:34,530
When you kept telling me
to keep them on,

332
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:36,230
I thought something was strange.

333
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:40,640
I will give you
your heels next time.

334
00:21:41,100 --> 00:21:43,040
You must be tired,
so get plenty of rest.

335
00:21:43,370 --> 00:21:46,080
If you do not start feeling better,
be sure to stop by the clinic.

336
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:48,180
Take care.

337
00:21:52,550 --> 00:21:54,990
Dr. Ju, those are not mine.

338
00:21:55,790 --> 00:21:57,250
They belong to Da Mi.

339
00:22:11,970 --> 00:22:13,740
Giving them to me as my physician...

340
00:22:14,740 --> 00:22:16,540
He really is a thoughtful doctor.

341
00:22:25,550 --> 00:22:26,850
- I am home.
- Welcome back.

342
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:27,920
I am home.

343
00:22:28,450 --> 00:22:29,620
You are still up.

344
00:22:30,120 --> 00:22:33,520
Why do you work this late?

345
00:22:33,660 --> 00:22:35,460
Do you have any idea
how worried I was,

346
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:36,890
my eldest grandson?

347
00:22:37,530 --> 00:22:38,530
I am sorry, Grandma.

348
00:22:38,660 --> 00:22:40,860
I had some work left to finish.
Please, sit down.

349
00:22:40,930 --> 00:22:42,100
Yes, all right.

350
00:22:44,870 --> 00:22:45,870
All right.

351
00:22:49,210 --> 00:22:50,970
- Seung Yun.
- Yes, Uncle?

352
00:22:51,040 --> 00:22:52,040
Your grandmother...

353
00:22:52,380 --> 00:22:55,080
was asking for you
all evening today.

354
00:22:55,450 --> 00:22:56,710
Try to come home early sometimes...

355
00:22:56,780 --> 00:22:59,150
and spend some time with her.

356
00:23:00,650 --> 00:23:02,490
Yes, I will keep that
in mind, Uncle.

357
00:23:03,820 --> 00:23:07,090
Do Yun is back too, Mother.
Mother, Do Yun also...

358
00:23:07,660 --> 00:23:10,390
worked late at the office
and came home together with him.

359
00:23:12,260 --> 00:23:13,400
It is okay, Mom.

360
00:23:18,800 --> 00:23:21,200
Jun Sung. My son,

361
00:23:21,710 --> 00:23:25,580
why are you so late?
I was waiting for you,

362
00:23:25,780 --> 00:23:27,840
craning my neck looking out for you.

363
00:23:28,950 --> 00:23:31,650
Did you eat?

364
00:23:36,320 --> 00:23:37,650
Grandma, it is me, Seung Yun.

365
00:23:38,760 --> 00:23:39,760
Seung Yun?

366
00:23:40,160 --> 00:23:41,790
Yes, your eldest grandson,
Seung Yun.

367
00:23:44,030 --> 00:23:46,460
My eldest grandson...

368
00:23:47,030 --> 00:23:48,530
It was Seung Yun.

369
00:23:49,830 --> 00:23:52,600
Father, I think it would be better
if Grandma went to bed.

370
00:23:53,700 --> 00:23:57,510
Mother, it is very late.
Let us go in.

371
00:23:59,280 --> 00:24:02,410
I will get your bed ready. Here.

372
00:24:02,650 --> 00:24:03,710
Careful, careful.

373
00:24:10,750 --> 00:24:13,620
I think Grandma got exhausted
waiting for us.

374
00:24:13,990 --> 00:24:15,090
Do not worry too much.

375
00:24:15,730 --> 00:24:17,030
She has days like this sometimes.

376
00:24:17,960 --> 00:24:21,930
He is right, Seung Yun.
I was worried she might get worse,

377
00:24:22,270 --> 00:24:24,940
but her progression
seems to have slowed down.

378
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:28,240
Let us just be grateful for that.

379
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:31,210
Still, I wish her condition...

380
00:24:31,270 --> 00:24:33,610
would improve even more, Aunt.

381
00:24:34,910 --> 00:24:38,680
Of course, if she could get better,
how wonderful would that be?

382
00:24:38,820 --> 00:24:40,720
I feel the exact same way.

383
00:24:42,250 --> 00:24:43,950
Let us find a way together, okay?

384
00:24:44,650 --> 00:24:46,220
Do not be so down.

385
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:48,290
Okay, I will.

386
00:24:56,830 --> 00:24:57,900
Yes, customer?

387
00:24:59,370 --> 00:25:00,370
Hello?

388
00:25:01,540 --> 00:25:03,170
Sorry, wrong number.

389
00:25:08,550 --> 00:25:10,450
What? Was it really a wrong number?

390
00:25:11,820 --> 00:25:12,820
What was that?

391
00:25:13,520 --> 00:25:15,920
She went completely quiet,
so I thought something happened,

392
00:25:15,990 --> 00:25:16,990
but she hasn't a care in the world.

393
00:25:20,320 --> 00:25:21,320
Wait.

394
00:25:22,160 --> 00:25:24,330
Wait, why am I worrying
about that rich brat?

395
00:25:24,560 --> 00:25:25,760
I have got enough problems
of my own.

396
00:25:28,970 --> 00:25:29,970
What is wrong with me?

397
00:25:33,970 --> 00:25:35,370
Hold on, Hak Sung.

398
00:25:36,110 --> 00:25:37,110
What is it?

399
00:25:37,410 --> 00:25:38,410
Go return...

400
00:25:39,210 --> 00:25:40,240
this money to your mother.

401
00:25:41,210 --> 00:25:43,650
The 10,000 dollars
my mother gave us?

402
00:25:44,080 --> 00:25:46,280
Since when do you turn down money?

403
00:25:47,350 --> 00:25:49,620
After thinking about it all night,

404
00:25:49,990 --> 00:25:53,120
taking the money and moving out
like we're being chased away...

405
00:25:53,390 --> 00:25:55,430
Like we are being chased away,
then what?

406
00:25:56,830 --> 00:25:58,330
It feels too unfair. I cannot do it.

407
00:25:59,660 --> 00:26:02,130
Honestly, are we even in a position
to feel aggrieved?

408
00:26:02,330 --> 00:26:04,470
You heard what the kids' mom
said, too.

409
00:26:04,970 --> 00:26:07,970
She told us not to cross paths
in her neighborhood.

410
00:26:08,670 --> 00:26:09,670
Aren't you scared?

411
00:26:10,210 --> 00:26:11,410
Because I am.

412
00:26:12,580 --> 00:26:15,750
I'm scared too, but I'm not going
to let it stop me.

413
00:26:16,150 --> 00:26:18,580
I'm going to stand tall
and push forward with my plans,

414
00:26:18,650 --> 00:26:19,650
so don't try to stop me.

415
00:26:20,280 --> 00:26:22,490
Ji Young, what are you thinking?

416
00:26:24,050 --> 00:26:27,620
I'm talking about your mother.
She may have cast you and me out,

417
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:29,730
but she will take our Ye Ri in.

418
00:26:29,960 --> 00:26:33,430
Ye Ri has every right
to inherit your mother's fortune.

419
00:26:34,970 --> 00:26:37,070
- What?
- Am I wrong?

420
00:26:37,230 --> 00:26:40,370
Ye Ri is your mother's
biological granddaughter.

421
00:26:40,440 --> 00:26:41,440
She's flesh and blood.

422
00:26:56,990 --> 00:26:58,720
(Mission: Mompossible)

423
00:27:15,110 --> 00:27:17,510
- The reason I came today, honey...
- Honey?

424
00:27:17,670 --> 00:27:20,480
- No, I mean...
- Goodness, what on earth...

425
00:27:20,580 --> 00:27:23,510
What's wrong with Da Mi?
She's doing fine at Mi Seon's place.

426
00:27:23,680 --> 00:27:25,720
You don't remember
the hurtful things you said, do you?

427
00:27:25,880 --> 00:27:29,550
Would my life be less exhausting
if Da Mi moved back in?

428
00:27:29,750 --> 00:27:31,090
You're still not ready?

429
00:27:31,220 --> 00:27:33,160
Some of the samples
are currently unaccounted for.

430
00:27:33,390 --> 00:27:35,830
I'm sorry, CEO Jeon. I'll go check
and look for them again.

431
00:27:36,430 --> 00:27:38,600
Do you really think stealing
a few samples...

432
00:27:38,800 --> 00:27:41,060
will be enough to get rid of her?

433
00:27:41,730 --> 00:27:43,730
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
